# Clear Glass gig file (clearglass.gig/1) — load it in Settings → Autofill → Gig, or in the gig panel.
format: clearglass.gig/1
platform: fiverr
title: I will write automated tests for your Node.js or JavaScript project
category: Programming & Tech
subcategory: QA & Review
tags:
  - unit testing
  - node.js
  - test automation
  - qa
  - javascript
description: >-
  Afraid every change might break something? I write automated tests that catch it first, so you can
  change your code with confidence.


  My own project has hundreds of test suites, run on every change. I write tests that check what the
  code is supposed to do, including the ways it can fail, not just the happy path.


  What you get:

  - Tests for your most important code paths and edge cases

  - A one-command test run, with a clear pass and fail report

  - A list of bugs the tests found, with how to reproduce each

  - Optional: tests running automatically on GitHub


  How it works: tell me what your project does and what scares you most about changing it. I start
  there, show you the first tests running, and build out from that.


  Works with plain Node.js, Jest, Mocha or Node's built-in test runner.
packages:
  basic:
    name: Starter Tests
    description: Tests for one module or feature, with a run command.
    deliveryDays: 2
    revisions: 1
    price: 50
  standard:
    name: Core Coverage
    description: Tests for your main features and failure cases, plus a bug list.
    deliveryDays: 5
    revisions: 2
    price: 150
  premium:
    name: Full Test Setup
    description: Broad coverage, CI on GitHub, and a guide to adding tests.
    deliveryDays: 9
    revisions: 3
    price: 350
faq:
  - question: Which test tools do you use?
    answer: Whatever your project already uses. If none, Node's built-in test runner or Jest.
  - question: Will you fix the bugs you find?
    answer: I list them with steps to reproduce. Fixing them can be added to the order.
  - question: Do you need my whole codebase?
    answer: Yes, or the part to be tested, with how to run it.
requirements:
  - What does your project do, and which part are you most worried about breaking?
  - Who will use it, and on what? (Windows, Mac, a server; one person or a team)
  - What must it always do, and what must it never do?
  - How will you check that it is done? (the test you will run, or what you will look at)
  - Please share any files, examples, access or data I need to start.
